Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
 cmake (>= 3.16),
 g++,
 pkg-config
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/kutuso/libmempressure
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libmempressure0
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Memory-pressure events from kernel PSI for applications
 libmempressure turns the kernel's Pressure Stall Information (PSI)
 into application-level memory-pressure events: a Linux answer to
 Android's onTrimMemory(). Instead of being killed by the OOM killer,
 applications learn that memory is getting tight and shed caches
 gracefully.

Package: libmempressure-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: libmempressure0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Development files for libmempressure
 Headers (C and the header-only C++ binding), the pkg-config file and
 the versioned symlink needed to build applications against
 libmempressure.
